<title>USA: Dauphin Technology buys founder's shares.</title>
<headline>Dauphin Technology buys founder's shares.</headline>
<dateline>PALATINE, Ill. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dauphin Technology Inc said it purchased all shares owned by Alan Yong, founder and former president of the company, and Yong resigned from the board.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the transaction, the company purchased more than 745,000 shares from Yong and his family, and Yong resigned from the board and terminated his involvement with the company, Dauphin said. Additional terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
